evening everyone welcome to the next  revolution I'm Steve Hilton and this is  the home of positive populism pro-worker  pro-family Pro community and especially  pro America important show tonight  coronavirus the economy and the  blue-collar boom 2020 latest that  outrageous Chuck Schumer business last  week we also have an unbelievable loony  left for you and of course a new Joe  Biden comedy segment with me live in Los  Angeles for the hour Adam Carolla and  Tammy Bruce Jenner Ellis and Taryn  Figaro they'll be joining us tonight as  well  all right there they are and here we go  we'll get to coronavirus in a second but  let's start positive we saw an  incredible jobs report on Friday two  hundred and seventy three thousand new  jobs in February almost a hundred  thousand more than expected  another 85,000 on top of that with  revisions to the previous two months  totals it's not just a number it's over  a third of a million Americans working  who weren't before just in the last few  weeks unemployment at a 50-year low  earnings continued to grow now if we  want this success to continue we have to  understand why it's happening the policy  foundations the Trump haters say it's  all thanks to Obama Barack Obama  literally saved the economy and the  benefits that we're seeing now from  Trump they are though they're the ripple  effects there is a narrative here that I  think is borne by the facts that suggest  that even if the overall numbers are  good they're not that much better or  substantially different from those under  Obama frankly these are Obama era policy  that allowed Trump to have two years it  was a gift it really was that is  dangerously wrong it means people will  think we can safely go back to Obama era  policies without hurting working  Americans that Trump just inherited a  good economy story is a lie and tonight  we'll show you the hard evidence it's  true that if you look at average  economic growth you see roughly the same  performance with Obama and Trump but  averages missed the life cycle of an  economic expansion it's much harder to  create growth in jobs at the end and the  beginning here's the pattern you  typically see growth is negative during  a recession it quickly accelerates to a  peak as the economy bounces back before  falling more gradually until then  next recession hits if the expansion  that followed the Great Recession the  Obama economy had lasted the same length  as the previous one we would have gone  into recession last June but we didn't  our economy kept growing so why did the  Trump economy not follow the pattern of  previous expansions perhaps because the  world economy was picking up speed  actually the rest of the world has been  slowing down Germany's GDP growth is  naught point five percent Japan's  naught point nine percent the  explanation and the policy lesson it's  so vital to learn is the change that  happened right there yes the 2016  election with the exception of one  quarter growth hasn't fallen below that  level since for three reasons  one a pro enterprise pro-business  approach that boosted business  confidence which translates into more  capital investment to deregulation  especially on energy which unleashed  American innovation and made America a  net exporter of oil for the first time  in 75 years three tax cuts for workers  but also employers so they can afford to  expand and invest creating more jobs and  higher productivity which enables higher  wages the trumpet haters say these  policies just help the rich that again  is a total lie the Trump boom is not a  one-percent boom is a blue-collar boom  look at earnings the haters say Trump is  just continuing the wage growth started  under Obama again you might believe this  if you look at the averages they say the  same on jobs and yes if you look at the  totals each month during both  administrations it seems like a  continuation but look behind the  averages here's how the top 25% and  bottom 25% did under Obama for much of  his time wage growth for the richest was  higher than wage growth for the poorest  by a wide margin now look at the picture  with Trump wage growth for the poorest  has been higher than for the richest  every month he's been in office and for  the first time in almost 10 years wage  growth for less skilled workers matched  wage growth for high-skilled workers  under Obama the rich got richer and the  poorest were stuck with Trump sure the  rich did well but the poorest and the  middle class are doing even better  look at household income in many ways  the most important measure in three  years with Trump household incomes have  gone up five times more than under eight  years of Obama and on jobs we're doing  far better than what you'd expect at  this stage of an expansion if you look  at the previous two expansions the  average monthly job gained during the  last year was 120,000 but over the last  year with Trump the average monthly gain  is 200 and 1,000 the monthly Trump job  gains are over 65 percent higher than  normal but it's also about the types of  jobs added the elitists laughed at Trump  when he said he'd bring back  manufacturing he just says well I'm no  I'm gonna negotiate a better deal well  hot what how exactly are you going to  negotiate that what magic wand do you  have what magic wand you have in 2018  more manufacturing jobs were added that  at any time for 30 years and we can  expect even more thanks to the new u.s.  MCA the most Pro worker trade deal in  history the point of all this is not to  praise any one politician but to explain  to all of them especially any  Republicans tempted to go back to  establishment economics after Trump  exactly what the policy mix is that most  helps those who are left behind by  globalization and open borders and here  we come to the central policy innovation  of the past three years pro-business on  tax and regulation pro-worker on trade  and immigration and in the end this is  delivered not just economic success but  something that strengthens our society  too that helps repair our torn social  fabric in the fourth quarter of last  year over 74 percent of people entering  the labor force came off the sidelines  the highest percentage since records  began that's the power of Trump's  blue-collar boom it lifts up the  Forgotten men and women left on the  scrap heap by the elitist policies of  the past all of this is put at risk by  Bernie or Biden just take one of the  central planks of the blue-collar boom  lower business taxes right now pretty  much whatever international measure you  pick it's the lowest here in America now  look where Biden wants to put it it  would lit  be the highest that is a disaster for  investment for jobs for household  incomes Bernie wants to take it to 35%  of course they both want to massively  raise taxes increased regulations closed  down domestic energy build up the  bureaucracy centralized power on and on  it goes  anti-worker anti-family anti-community  whether it's socialism with bernie or  the swamp with Biden it is a disaster  for America

